# Lidia's Heart (Q023), played by a level 64 character who completed Tragedy in von
# Hellmann's Forest (Q022, registered so its row loads):
# Innocentin starts it with the map and the silver key; the broken bookshelf gives the
# hairpin, then the diary; Innocentin's long talk stops at cond 5 ("No, I haven't read it"),
# reading the diary's last help page marks it read, and the talk goes on to cond 6; the tombstone
# wakes the ghost of von Hellmann, one at a time (a second tombstone talk sees it, and once
# it decays after 300 s the tombstone wakes another); the ghost takes the diary; digging at
# the tombstone takes 10 s and finds a second silver key; Violet, the box and Violet again
# complete the quest. Expectations are derived from the reference source
# (Q023_LidiasHeart.java, QuestState.setCond, Quest.addSpawn, RequestBypassToServer).
trace internal/gameserver/script/testdata/oracle/scenarios/q023_lidias_heart.golden
character Lidia 64
quest Q022_TragedyInVonHellmannForest <state>=COMPLETED
script quest.Q022_TragedyInVonHellmannForest
script quest.Q023_LidiasHeart
item 7063 7064 7148 7149 7150
page villagemaster/31328.htm
page default/31526.htm
page default/31524.htm
page default/31523.htm
page merchant/31386.htm
page default/31530.htm
page script/quest/Q023_LidiasHeart/
page help/lidias_diary/
npc innocentin 31328 VillageMasterPriest 10 0 0
npc bookshelf 31526 Folk -10 0 0
npc ghost 31524 Folk 0 10 0
npc tombstone 31523 Folk 0 -10 0
npc violet 31386 Merchant 20 20 0
npc box 31530 Folk -20 -20 0

# Innocentin: his quest window lists both his quests (the completed Q022 first); Q022 is
# completed and the level is 64, so Lidia's Heart may start.
action innocentin
action innocentin
  S ActionFailed
  S NpcHtmlMessage obj=innocentin item=0 page=villagemaster/31328.htm
  S ActionFailed
